{"kind":"request","text":"@planner BO1 has one concrete admission-data gap in ruling 7a2beda6. Rules@10's application-install-identities retains only { destination, archive } for requirements (platform/src/device-application-rules.ts). application-stage-definitions sends name, declarations, definitionTextN, needsArchive, definition, job, release, semantic digest and additions (application-install.ts). It never sends needsCommons or the package semantic bytes. PlatformReceive fields cannot be ValuePlace (contract/platform.ts), so Directory@22 cannot fetch those semantic bytes through the declared receive seam. A directory has-commons guard cannot honestly tell a commons-requiring package from an ordinary one using that message.\n\nPlease adopt a versioned path that carries the requirement, or revise the native guard acceptance. A new Rules version with its existing proof-derived requirement storage and application-stage send extended to needsCommons appears necessary; that would also change the new cohort and catalog count beyond 84. We will not change Rules@10's historical meaning, invent Rules@11 (already a historical pin), or accept a host boolean as native evidence without a ruling. The independent reference, cohort creation, note, codec and host-precheck work is progressing under promise ca05c3f0.","body":{"conditions":"Resolve the immutable Rules@10 to Directory@22 admission-data gap before implementing the native commons-missing guard. Independent BO1 work continues.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}